// The editor's own half of the game seam.
//
// The engine asks a *game* for these (docs/IDML.md §2). The editor is not a game
// -- it hosts other people's -- so it answers as a host: a `@name` in a previewed
// document reads that document's own variable, which is what makes a gate like
// `?@ready` mean anything in the panel.
//
// It is imported instead of `stub/`, whose g_ref answers 0 for everything. That
// was correct for a unit test and wrong here: it hid every gated panel in every
// game the editor opened, which looked like the UI having broken.
//
// The legacy reader is scr_get because the games the editor still opens are
// documents the engine interprets. When they become `id`, this becomes a lookup
// into the previewed program instead -- and the editor will have to run it.

g_ref(string name) {
} return int scr_get(0 - 1, name);

g_act(string name) {
  lset((import ed_st), 17, 1);
} return void;

g_stage(int k) {
} return int ed_gstage(k);
